            <div xml:id="d247">

                <pb facs="0292" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">033.5511/160: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Rear Admiral Long to the Secretary of the Navy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >U.S.S. “George Washington,”</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1919-09-29T21:35:00-04:00"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September 29, 1919,9.35
                        p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>The following is for the Secretary of State:</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Re</hi> your 011928. I am directed by His Majesty to
                    inform you that it is very agreeable to him to make a tour of the United States
                    before visiting the President at Washington. His Majesty fully appreciates the
                    changed conditions and regrets extremely to hear of the President’s illness. I
                    am directed by His Majesty to inform you that in view of intended schedule he
                    would greatly prefer to arrive at Hoboken, N. J., on Thursday the 2d instead of
                    Friday the 3d. As soon as possible, he requests that a detailed program of the
                    visit in New York be forwarded. (Two groups garbled.) 180329.</p>
                <closer>[No signature indicated]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
